    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nOpening large files directly with nvim + mini.starter causes unnecessary slowdown\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0-dev-2218+ga757195a6-dirty\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `yes mini | head -n 500000 > example-file`\r\n2. `nvim example-file`\r\n\r\nThis takes starter around 30ms to check if there is something shown\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nrun checks in reverse order to speed up process (args, buffers, lines)\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nprocessing time of M.is_something_shown is slow\r\nwith large json files (~18M, ~750000 lines) it takes around 150ms (according to lazy.nvim profiler) ",
